# exp_10 yaw_pilot — Coder round 9 (post-closure, test-only): PATH shims must not live under a path containing `os.pathsep`

Coder = Claude Opus 5 in `/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt10` (branch `exp10-yaw-pilot`; `git merge main` first — main is at `fcf7413` or later). Scope: ONLY `tests/test_exp10_record_tools.py` (and `tests/exp10_record_fixture.py` if the shim helper lives there). No change to any tool or script; the exp_10 record is closed and approved. TDD; small commits prefixed `exp_10 round 9:`; Opus trailer; no push/amend; no GPU; `ckpt/` read-only.

Problem (diagnosed by the Planner, 2026-09-28): the fault-injection tests of the finish script install `mv`/`cp` shims in `<scratch root>/test_bin` and prepend that directory to `PATH`. When pytest's basetemp path contains a colon (another session ran the suite with `--basetemp=/tmp/pytest-exp11-2026-09-28_07:55:15`), the shim directory is split at the colons by the shell and never found, so the real `mv`/`cp` run, the finish completes with rc 0, and 12 tests fail spuriously (`test_finish_restores_all_three_artefacts_when_a_publication_fails[*]`, `test_finish_removes_a_publication_it_created_when_the_next_one_fails`, `test_finish_rolls_back_all_three_artefacts_when_it_is_terminated`, `test_finish_keeps_an_artefacts_absence_when_it_is_terminated`, `test_finish_keeps_the_backups_when_the_rollback_itself_fails`, `test_finish_refuses_an_incomplete_rollback_copy[*]`, `test_finish_keeps_the_publication_when_it_is_terminated_while_backing_it_up[*]`, `test_finish_never_installs_a_rollback_copy_that_lost_its_marker`, `test_finish_completes_the_rollback_when_it_is_terminated_during_it`). Reproduced: `--basetemp=<dir with a colon>` → 2 failed; the same two tests with a colon-free basetemp → 2 passed. The finish script is not at fault.

Fix: make the shim location independent of the basetemp path — create the shim bin directory with `tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="exp10-shim-", dir=<a colon-free base>)` where the base is `/tmp` (or `$TMPDIR` if it contains no `os.pathsep`), register it for cleanup (fixture finalizer / `addfinalizer`), and assert loudly (`pytest.fail` with the offending path) if the chosen directory still contains `os.pathsep` or whitespace. Also add a regression test that runs one shim-based finish case with a scratch root whose path contains a colon (create it explicitly under tmp_path, e.g. `tmp_path / "with:colon"`) and asserts the shim fires (rc != 0 / 143 as the case requires). Keep every other test unchanged.

Verification to report: `python -m pytest tests/test_exp10_record_tools.py -q -p no:cacheprovider` with a normal basetemp AND with `--basetemp="<scratchpad>/pt_colon_09:00:00"` (both must be fully green); `git diff --check`; scope (`git diff --name-only <merge-base> HEAD`); py_compile. Final report: SHAs, summary lines, deviations.
"""Pytest configuration for the xRIR test suite.

The project is used as a plain source tree (no installed package), so the repository
root is prepended to ``sys.path``.  ``XRIR_DATA_PATH`` is defaulted to the local
AcousticRooms cache: ``treble_multi_room_dataset.treble_xRIR_dataset`` reads that
variable *at import time*, so it has to be set before any test imports the dataset.
An externally provided value always wins, and the fallback is applied only when that
directory actually exists, so the suite stays portable to machines without the cache.
"""
import os
import sys

_REPO_ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
if _REPO_ROOT not in sys.path:
    sys.path.insert(0, _REPO_ROOT)

_DATA_CACHE_FALLBACK = "/home/yixunhu/data_cache/AcousticRooms"
if "XRIR_DATA_PATH" not in os.environ and os.path.isdir(_DATA_CACHE_FALLBACK):
    os.environ["XRIR_DATA_PATH"] = _DATA_CACHE_FALLBACK


def pytest_collection_modifyitems(items):
    """The pinned exp_03 live acceptance record requires two visible GPUs."""
    import pytest
    import torch

    target = os.path.join(_REPO_ROOT, 'tests', 'test_exp03_record_tools.py')
    for item in items:
        if (os.path.realpath(str(item.fspath)) == target and
                item.nodeid.split('::')[-1] == 'test_skipping_the_gate_recomputation_is_not_acceptance' and
                torch.cuda.device_count() < 2):
            item.add_marker(pytest.mark.skip(reason='exp_03 live environment requires two visible GPUs'))
